Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:21:14 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fail loudly when setXCom is given a Scala type or empty
 object

SetXCom and task-state values go through Frame, which converts the
message object with Jackson. A Scala collection, Option or case class
was stored as bean properties or as {}, and the task succeeded.

Inspect the original value first. Reject Scala types (detected by a
scala. name prefix on the class, superclasses or interfaces, with no
Scala dependency) and objects Jackson would encode as {}. Java types
that already encoded usefully still pass through unchanged.

related: #66329

